{title: Footsteps of Jesus}
{artist: Mary B. C. Slade / Asa B. Everett}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: D}
{key_original: Eb}
{tempo: 110}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Church Hymnal (Cleveland, Tennessee: Tennessee Music & Publishing, 1951), p. 47)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Sweetly, Lord, have we [G]heard Thee call[D]ing,
[D]Come, follow [A]Me!
[D]And we see where Thy [G]footprints fall[D]ing
[Bm]Lead [A7]us to [D]Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Footprints of Je__[D]__sus,
[D]That make the pathway [A]glow;
[D]We will follow the [G]steps of Je[D]sus
[Bm]Wher[A7]e’er they [D]go.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Though they lead o’er the [G]cold, dark mount[D]ains,
[D]Seeking His [A]sheep;
[D]Or along by Si[G]loam’s fount[D]ains,
[Bm]Help[A7]ing the [D]weak.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]If they lead through the [G]temple ho[D]ly,
[D]Preaching the [A]Word;
[D]Or in homes of the [G]poor and low[D]ly,
[Bm]Serv[A7]ing the [D]Lord.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]Though, dear Lord, in Thy [G]pathway keep[D]ing,
[D]We follow [A]Thee;
[D]Through the gloom of that [G]place of weep[D]ing,
[Bm]Geth[A7]sema[D]ne!
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[D]If Thy way and its [G]sorrows bear[D]ing,
[D]We go a[A]gain,
[D]Up the slope of the [G]hillside, bear[D]ing
[Bm]Our [A7]cross of [D]pain.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
[D]By and by, through the [G]shining por[D]tals,
[D]Turning our [A]feet,
[D]We shall walk, with the [G]glad immor[D]tals,
[Bm]Heav’n’s [A7]golden [D]street.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 7}
[D]Then at last when on [G]high He sees [D]us,
[D]Our journey [A]done,
[D]We will rest where the [G]steps of Je[D]sus
[Bm]End [A7]at His [D]throne.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
